01:54:57.400 --> 01:54:58.340
God rest his soul.

01:54:58.500 --> 01:54:59.740
You haven't tried the grog yet, pilot.

01:55:03.930 --> 01:55:12.460
We make it ourselves, by the barrel, rice, fruit, water, and then we let it ferment, and then we put it in this stew we made.

01:55:13.100 --> 01:55:18.700
Of course, it'd be better if we let it sit for a year or two to mellow, but as fast as we make it, we drink it.

01:55:18.940 --> 01:55:20.360
I'll let the pilot talk.

01:55:20.740 --> 01:55:22.000
Yes, yes, you talk.

01:55:23.600 --> 01:55:26.740
When I saw him out there, I thought he was one of the monkeys drinking like that.

01:55:28.400 --> 01:55:29.900
Perhaps you prefer healing ways now, pilot.

01:55:30.540 --> 01:55:31.320
Are those real swords?

01:55:31.970 --> 01:55:32.950
Yes, they're real enough.

01:55:33.940 --> 01:55:34.860
We're not allowed weapons.

01:55:35.640 --> 01:55:36.780
How do you get to carry swords?

01:55:37.220 --> 01:55:39.730
You haven't changed, Jan Roper, have you?

01:55:41.460 --> 01:55:41.840
Who are they?

01:55:42.740 --> 01:55:43.660
Our Toxies pilot.

01:55:45.340 --> 01:55:46.400
Cast a button a week.

01:55:46.610 --> 01:55:47.430
They rattle like stuff.

01:55:48.040 --> 01:55:49.340
Plenty of figure and no pucks.

01:55:49.670 --> 01:55:50.550
You want one, pilot?

01:55:51.520 --> 01:55:54.220
Take your choice and use my bunk.

01:55:54.560 --> 01:55:56.580
The pilot doesn't want one of our harlots.

01:55:57.330 --> 01:55:58.050
He's got his own.

01:55:58.400 --> 01:55:58.860
Hey, pilot?

01:56:04.160 --> 01:56:05.920
Listen, has anyone seen the ship?

01:56:06.630 --> 01:56:12.290
Aye, it's in the harbor, careened and scraped and cleaned, as if she'd been built yesterday.

01:56:12.850 --> 01:56:17.780
The rigging's perfect, and the sails, see the sails?

01:56:18.010 --> 01:56:18.410
What about them?

01:56:19.240 --> 01:56:22.390
They've made them out of silk, strong as canvas.

01:56:23.630 --> 01:56:27.030
She's ready to sail on the tide tonight, if need be.

01:56:27.380 --> 01:56:28.240
Are we leaving, pilot?

01:56:29.560 --> 01:56:29.960
Is there any...

01:56:30.000 --> 01:56:33.010
enemy shipping in the waters. Are there any prizes to be taken?

01:56:34.000 --> 01:56:36.250
Prize beyond your dreams. Prize?

01:56:36.760 --> 01:56:39.640
What prize, pilot? The Jesuit black ship.

01:56:40.200 --> 01:56:42.420
She's worth millions in gold. Gold?

01:56:42.980 --> 01:56:45.080
Then we'll be rich. I need papers to kill.

01:56:45.200 --> 01:56:46.170
Good. Very good.

01:56:46.980 --> 01:56:49.440
We'll see you on the pilot. There's six on us now.

01:56:49.600 --> 01:56:51.570
There will be a way. Do you want to eat, pilot?

01:56:51.670 --> 01:56:52.770
We've got some lovely roast.

01:56:54.030 --> 01:56:55.670
You've been staying with us, pilot. There's plenty of room.

01:56:55.830 --> 01:56:57.010
Have some more grab. Yeah.

01:56:57.410 --> 01:56:58.310
Oh, yeah.

01:57:00.000 --> 01:57:02.400
And now you're back. Our prayers are answered.

01:57:02.660 --> 01:57:04.020
Three cheers for the pilot.

01:57:04.220 --> 01:57:04.540
Hit me.

01:57:17.410 --> 01:57:17.890
I'm good.

01:57:31.950 --> 01:57:32.810
God curse!

01:57:37.960 --> 01:57:39.630
No, nondeska anji-sa?

01:57:40.270 --> 01:57:42.980
Oh furrow, ima wakaremasuka?

01:57:44.430 --> 01:57:44.950
Furrow!

01:58:24.130 --> 01:58:29.680
It you are, Mariko-san. Gladens my heart to see you.

01:58:31.150 --> 01:58:33.090
Lord Taranaga has sent for us.

01:58:33.260 --> 01:58:35.320
I know. When can I speak to thee?

01:58:37.240 --> 01:58:39.200
That is very difficult now, Anji-san.

01:58:40.230 --> 01:58:42.010
It was difficult before, but we did.

01:58:42.250 --> 01:58:45.800
I'm sorry, but we must go now.

01:58:58.380 --> 01:58:59.460
Which you are, Taranaga-sama.

01:59:00.410 --> 01:59:00.830
Sit down, Anjin.

01:59:03.440 --> 01:59:17.830
Have you seen the workers?

01:59:23.420 --> 01:59:29.620
Only five of them are left.

01:59:30.000 --> 01:59:31.440
The two of them are dead.

01:59:33.940 --> 01:59:38.030
I'm here to summon my son Suga and his wife.

01:59:38.850 --> 01:59:42.300
Please translate the rest of the story to Anjin.

01:59:44.050 --> 01:59:45.310
Yes, sir.

01:59:52.010 --> 01:59:57.540
However, you will not be able to say a word.

02:00:01.400 --> 02:00:03.000
But you must not speak at all.

02:00:05.320 --> 02:00:06.540
I understand, Mr. Duranaka.

02:00:18.070 --> 02:00:19.440
I've been to the Uchgata.

02:00:20.920 --> 02:00:21.340
Don't worry.

02:00:23.000 --> 02:00:23.540
I'm going to take a moment.

02:00:24.340 --> 02:00:24.640
It's good.

02:00:25.680 --> 02:00:25.900
Yes?

02:00:50.960 --> 02:00:53.230
Father, did you do something wrong?

02:00:54.370 --> 02:00:57.140
What do you mean wrong?

02:01:19.020 --> 02:01:24.420
The Lady Kenchiko says that whoever accused her husband is a liar.

02:01:27.730 --> 02:01:29.130
常にわしの命令に従っておったと申すのか。

02:01:31.730 --> 02:01:37.760
My master asks, if Rodis has always obeyed orders, and Rodis has always said, always.

02:01:41.340 --> 02:01:59.830
My master has ordered them to put their children to death.

02:02:14.910 --> 02:02:15.050
That's it!

02:03:03.520 --> 02:03:07.640
My children, there are no children, my father.

02:03:09.360 --> 02:03:12.760
My father, my father, has already been on a mission.

02:03:17.060 --> 02:03:19.320
Rhodes says that his children are gone.

02:03:24.700 --> 02:03:25.400
I'm not alone.

02:03:29.330 --> 02:03:29.590
Actually,

02:03:31.340 --> 02:03:35.970
I wanted to make sure that those people were able to make sure that they were able to make sure that they were in this situation.

02:03:40.640 --> 02:03:48.630
Lord Tuanaga says that the children are safe. My master needs to be sure of both Lord Suga and Lady Genjiko.

02:03:49.620 --> 02:03:53.570
The master says that foul times require foul taste.

02:04:10.840 --> 02:04:11.100
Come here, kids.

02:04:22.770 --> 02:04:23.210
Yes, yes, yes.

02:04:25.920 --> 02:04:27.670
Oh, soldier.

02:04:31.790 --> 02:04:35.660
Come on, get out of the way.

02:04:36.110 --> 02:04:50.900
Get out of the way.

02:05:04.920 --> 02:05:10.450
Mariko, you may leave. Anjin will stay here.

02:05:42.960 --> 02:05:44.240
You can try to open it.

02:05:44.420 --> 02:05:45.740
I see.

02:06:03.740 --> 02:06:05.280
I understand you wanted to see me, pilot.

02:06:07.980 --> 02:06:08.220
Yes.

02:06:21.010 --> 02:06:29.980
I want your holy oath.

02:06:30.060 --> 02:06:32.680
That what you hear now will never be repeated.

02:06:34.620 --> 02:06:37.160
Or nothing will be said.

02:06:39.020 --> 02:06:40.000
Perhaps that might be better.

02:06:42.760 --> 02:06:43.560
But you have my oath.

02:06:44.100 --> 02:06:45.160
Then let me hear it before God.

02:06:48.120 --> 02:06:49.580
I solemnly swear before God,

02:06:49.980 --> 02:06:51.860
what I hear now shall never pass my lips again.

02:06:53.160 --> 02:06:55.890
Nor shall you write it down, nor convey it in any fashion.

02:06:56.940 --> 02:06:57.380
Swear to that.

02:06:59.400 --> 02:06:59.960
As you have just...

02:07:00.090 --> 02:07:01.210
spoken, so do I swear.

02:07:03.400 --> 02:07:13.300
Maja, humbly ask that you grant a divorce to the Lady Toda.

02:07:16.830 --> 02:07:18.570
Humbly ask for her hand in marriage.

02:07:28.770 --> 02:07:29.980
Ask him in my...

02:07:54.260 --> 02:07:55.660
words

02:08:01.650 --> 02:08:08.910
That is a very presumptuous request, though Toranaga forbid you to ever speak of it again.

02:08:09.090 --> 02:08:13.740
That is all.

02:08:18.680 --> 02:08:19.560
Anjite, Kinzel!

02:08:26.870 --> 02:08:27.290
Toranaga様.

02:08:30.892 --> 02:08:31.892
Who is it?
